# TypeScript/TSX Conventions

- Prefer explicit function signatures and exported API types; avoid `any`.
- Use meaningful, descriptive names (no 1–2 letter vars). Prefer full words.
- Use early returns; avoid deep nesting and unnecessary try/catch.
- Keep controllers thin; move business logic to use-cases.
- Domain code must not import infrastructure (enforce clean architecture boundaries).
- Keep comments minimal and insightful; avoid obvious comments.
- Use multi-line formatting over dense one-liners; wrap long lines.
- Match existing project formatting; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Frontend: keep presentational components pure; fetch in hooks/services.
- Backend: DTOs for IO boundaries; value-objects encapsulate invariants.

